Z||000000||85ZainoGT||11-11-2001||12:34 AM||||my power windows, well the drivers side makes some interesting noises, but works fine, but the passenger side is slowwwww. anyway to fix it? price?  thanks!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1987 Gold GT 2.8L<BR>All the options :)<BR>  pics are coming :)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||11-11-2001||05:57 AM||||Try greasing the motor.  If that doesn't work, you could always replace the motor.  I think they're only about $60.  A real PITA to change though.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-11-2001||12:35 PM||||Before messing with the motor, grease the guide and lift tracks, the rollers that run in those tracks, and the big counter spring. <P>Spread the spring coils with a screw driver to make sure the grease gets inside. Wipe up whatever squeezes out of the coils...<P>Grease the teeth on the lifting gear as well.<P>If it's still slow after that then the motor may need more work or replacement.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
